bc250: opt-in CH7218 DP-to-HDMI 2.1 adapter quirk

Some DP to HDMI 2.1 adapters built on a Chrontel CH7218 ship firmware that
misreports the downstream port: it clears DP_DOWNSTREAMPORT_PRESENT, or
reports the detailed downstream port as DP, while the device identity and
the EDID describe a DP to HDMI 2.1 PCON. DC then classifies the adapter
DISPLAY_DONGLE_NONE, never runs FRL negotiation, and sends 4K90/4K120 as
DP RGB that the adapter cannot emit over TMDS. The sink stays black. 4K60
still works, which is what makes it look like a mode problem rather than a
detection problem.

Found, diagnosed and originally written by @dejan_994.

Reported against a UGREEN DP to HDMI 2.1 adapter, DPCD branch OUI 2B:02:F0,
branch name CH7218, on a BC-250 driving an HDMI 2.1 TV. A Cable Matters
102101 on the same board does not need this: it already identifies as an
HDMI converter.

Behind amdgpu.bc250_ch7218_quirk, DEFAULT OFF, and that is the point of the
patch rather than a detail of it. Healthy CH7218 units report themselves
correctly, nothing in the DPCD tells an affected unit from a healthy one,
and applying the quirk unconditionally would override correct information
from a working adapter. Every entry point starts with the same gate, so
with the parameter unset the driver behaves exactly as it would without
this patch. bc250_hdmi21 is required as well, since the quirk restores
HDMI 2.1 PCON ceilings that mean nothing when PCON support is off.

With the quirk enabled and a CH7218 present:

  - force DISPLAY_DONGLE_DP_HDMI_CONVERTER at the two points where the
    firmware's misreport would otherwise produce DISPLAY_DONGLE_NONE
  - restore the documented ceilings: 12 bpc, FRL 48 Gbps, YCbCr 4:2:2 and
    4:2:0 pass-through
  - re-assert those ceilings after the DFP capability extension is parsed,
    which would otherwise overwrite them with the firmware's own values
  - restore DP_DSC_SUPPORT when firmware clears the bit while still
    returning a populated DSC decoder capability block

Not done, deliberately. No DP_BRANCH_DEVICE_ID_2B02F0 added to
ddc_service_types.h: 7.2 already defines it and 7.3-rc does not, so touching
that header would either duplicate a define or make the two patch sets
diverge. A file-local constant avoids both. No FreeSync PCON allowlist
entry either: 7.2 already lists the ID, 7.3-rc uses a different structure
for the same thing, and the reporter states VRR does not work on this
adapter regardless, so it would be an ungateable change to a static table
for no observed benefit.

DCN201 PCON support and the DSC engines are enabled by separate patches.

